  "behavior": [
    "Accumulator-address stores preserve live address and value aliases; the mandatory native fixture exercises widths, calls, and guarded memory.",
    "Narrow integer operations normalize significant bits and signed shifts correctly, including ABI carriers, while preserving the original input IR.",
    "Constant i128 pair stores preserve both words and adjacent memory.",
    "Bounded i128 arithmetic, comparisons, shifts and constant division/remainder lower through scalar word operations. Reusing generated words closes the unchanged Wyhash.hash and Wyhash.init emission rows.",
    "Immediate arithmetic and arithmetic shifts preserve live RCX sources and aliases in both typed and production dispatch. Rollback restores selector state.",
    "The i16 integration oracle accounts for truncation before the reverse shift; LLVM and both local routes agree on 0x0234 for (0x1234 << 4) >> 4.",
    "Native fixture counters, provenance hashes, and summaries derive from the shared population registry. The production runner passes all 35 populations; its failure path preserves the original error.",
    "The unchanged pinned upstream Fibonacci program executes all six assertions in ReleaseFast and ReleaseSmall with LLVM-equivalent exit status, stdout and stderr."
  ],
